  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["R51"],
      "pins": ["R51.1", "R51.2"],
      "nets": ["I2C2_SDA_FCC", "I2C2_SDA_NAVC", "I2C1_SDA_FCC"],
      "obs": "On the Connections sheet the I2C cross‑link between the two MCUs is built from two 0 Ω jumpers: R50 ties I2C1_SCL_FCC to I2C2_SCL_NAVC (correct), but R51 ties I2C2_SDA_FCC to I2C2_SDA_NAVC. The FCC‑side SDA jumper therefore uses the FCC I2C2 bus instead of the FCC I2C1 bus.",
      "expected": "The shared FCC↔NAVC I2C link must be a single coherent bus. The FCC sheet note states 'UART2, I2C1, and GPIO_A to GPIO_H -> NAVC' and the NAVC sheet note states 'I2C2_NAVC already pulled up by I2C1_FCC resistors!', i.e. both the SCL and the SDA jumpers should connect FCC I2C1 to NAVC I2C2. R51 should therefore be I2C1_SDA_FCC <-> I2C2_SDA_NAVC.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Connections sheet, I2C Connections block: 'I2C1_SCL_FCC -[R50 0]- ...' and 'I2C2_SDA_FCC -[R51 0]- ...' (page 4/6)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC sheet note: 'UART2, I2C1, and GPIO_A to GPIO_H -> NAVC'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NAVC sheet note: 'I2C2_NAVC already pulled up by I2C1_FCC resistors!'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "confirmed in Hades.sch: NAVC↔FCC run UART2 + I2C + GPIO between the two MCUs"}
      ],
      "impact": "The cross‑MCU I2C bus is split: the SCL line of the link is driven by FCC I2C1 while the SDA line is taken from FCC I2C2, so neither FCC I2C1 nor the NAVC I2C2 has a matching SCL/SDA pair on the link. The FCC and NAVC cannot exchange I2C traffic, breaking the navigation‑solution transfer from NAVC to FCC.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All spec‑traceable parts, values and the documented barometer RESET/EOC swap match the drawing, but the FCC↔NAVC shared‑I2C link is inconsistent: the SDA jumper (R51) is wired to I2C2_SDA_FCC instead of I2C1_SDA_FCC, contradicting the FCC/NAVC sheet notes that define the shared bus as FCC I2C1 ↔ NAVC I2C2, which would break inter‑MCU I2C communication."
}

